{{ 'zhp-collection.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'zhp-collection.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}

<div class="zhp-wrapper">
  <section class="zhp-faq-section" id="faq">
    <div class="zhp-container">
      <div class="zhp-sec-header">
        <span class="zhp-sec-tag">QUESTIONS & ANSWERS</span>
        <h2 class="zhp-sec-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p class="zhp-sec-subtitle">
          Everything you need to know about choosing, playing, and caring for your Zavelyn instrument.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="zhp-faq-container">
        <div class="zhp-accordion">
          <!-- Q1: Beginner suitability -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item active">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="true">
              <span>Do I need prior musical experience or note-reading skills to play?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                <strong>No musical experience is needed.</strong> Every tongue on our drums is tuned to mathematically harmonious intervals, meaning there are no "wrong" or dissonant notes. In addition, each note tongue is laser-marked with a number that matches our included songbook. Complete beginners can play familiar melodies within their first 5 minutes of opening the box.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q2: Difference between Handpan and Steel Tongue Drum -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>What is the difference between a Handpan and a Steel Tongue Drum?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                A <strong>Handpan (or Pantam)</strong> like the <em>Zavelyn Handpan Master (22")</em> is hand-hammered from nitrided steel with dimpled acoustic tone fields on an expansive convex dome. It produces a soft, ethereal cathedral sustain primarily played with the pads of the thumbs and fingers. <strong>Steel Tongue Drums</strong> (Pro 15", Plus 11", Mini 6", Rain 3") feature precision laser-cut tongues that resonate deeply when struck with either the included rubber mallets or finger picks.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q3: Which model is right for me? -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Which model should I choose as my first drum?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                • <strong>Zavelyn Handpan Master (22"):</strong> Flagship concert instrument for sound practitioners, performers, and those seeking authentic handpan resonance.<br>
                • <strong>Zavelyn Drum Pro (15"):</strong> Our most popular steel tongue drum with 15 notes spanning two full octaves—ideal for adults seeking rich melodic range.<br>
                • <strong>Zavelyn Drum Plus (11"):</strong> Best-value everyday model with 11 notes—perfect balance of size, tone, and portable weight.<br>
                • <strong>Zavelyn Drum Mini (6"):</strong> Lightweight 8-note drum tailored for children, travel, and desk mindfulness.<br>
                • <strong>Zavelyn Rain Drum (3"):</strong> Compact weatherproof chime designed for outdoor gardens and sensory relaxation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q4: Included accessories -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>What accessories come included with each order?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                Every order arrives as a complete all-in-one kit. All models include custom-fitted travel bags or pouches, balanced mallets, and tutorial guides. The 22" Handpan Master additionally includes an adjustable aluminum tripod stand, heavy-duty travel backpack, and braided edge guard.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q5: Shipping times -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How fast is shipping, and how are instruments packaged?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                Orders are processed and dispatched within <strong>24 to 48 hours</strong> from our US fulfillment hubs. Shipping is <strong>free on all orders over $49</strong>. Every instrument is securely packed inside heavy-duty shock-absorbent foam enclosures to ensure it arrives in pristine, factory-calibrated tune.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q6: 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee & Returns -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How does the 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee work?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                We want you to experience acoustic harmony with complete confidence. You have <strong>60 days</strong> from the date of delivery to play and enjoy your instrument. If you are not completely delighted with its sound quality, touch, or finish, simply contact our US-based support team for an effortless return and 100% refund.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Q7: Care and maintenance -->
          <div class="zhp-faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="zhp-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How should I clean and maintain my instrument?</span>
              <span class="zhp-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="zhp-faq-answer">
              <p>
                Wipe your drum down after extended playing sessions with a clean microfiber cloth. For the nitrided Handpan Master, applying a thin drop of natural mineral or phoenix oil once a month preserves its rich satin patina and protects against ambient moisture. Keep instruments stored in their padded bags when not in use.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

